Modified versions must remain private and may not be distributed without prior written authorization.

3.2 Small Business Use

Small Businesses may use the Software free of charge for their internal business operations.

Authorized Small Businesses may:

* Install and execute the Software on company-owned or authorized devices.
* Inspect and audit the source code.
* Modify the Software for internal operational requirements.
* Maintain private internal builds.
* Deploy modified versions internally among authorized personnel.

Such permission does not authorize external distribution, resale, sublicensing, or publication of modified versions.

